(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff pulse train output command process image.
</summary>
<description>
Requires EL2521 enhanced mode, Standard 32-bit (MDP 253/511): RxPDOs 0x1601, 0x1607 and 0x1605.
Control bits 0, 1 and 2 select the base frequency, disable the ramp and start target travel.
Frequency preserves the UINT16 PDO bit pattern, including direction encoding selected through CoE.
In relative mode the interpreted command scales the selected base frequency by 1/32767; in direct mode
CoE 0x8010:16 multiplies the interpreted command in 0.01 Hz units. Frequency is not a 32-bit Hz value.
TargetCounterValue is a separate 32-bit target; SetCounterValue presets encoder feedback.
Link fields individually; this aggregate is not a packed wire buffer. Configure CoE before enabling outputs.
Use one owner task; externally synchronize other access. Copies do not create links or an atomic snapshot.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE PULSE_TRAIN_OUTPUT_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	Control AT %Q* : WORD;
	//! <summary>Raw frequency command at 0x7010:11; interpretation follows CoE scaling and sign representation.</summary>
	Frequency AT %Q* : UINT;
	//! <summary>32-bit target at 0x7010:12, transmitted by PTO Target PDO 0x1607.</summary>
	TargetCounterValue AT %Q* : UDINT;
	//! <summary>ENC control from PDO 0x1605; bit 2 requests setting the feedback counter.</summary>
	CounterControl AT %Q* : WORD;
	//! <summary>Counter preset at 0x7020:11, accepted through CounterControl bit 2.</summary>
	SetCounterValue AT %Q* : UDINT;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
